The reader also offers OpenDyslexic 2.001 by Abelardo Gonzalez, whose
regular face ships unmodified inside the Readium navigator as
readium/fonts/OpenDyslexic-Regular.otf. The reader bundles the matching
OpenDyslexic-Italic.otf, -Bold.otf and -BoldItalic.otf, also unmodified,
in reader/src/main/assets/fonts/. All four are identical to the files
of the same names under otf/ in
https://github.com/antijingoist/open-dyslexic/tree/03aa68333abaef14718091a46bff52794b34cf39
Their glyphs derive from Bitstream Vera Sans, Copyright (c) 2003 by
Bitstream, Inc., under the Bitstream Vera license, and OpenDyslexic's
changes and additional glyphs are licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution 3.0 Unported. Both ship beside the fonts as
LICENSE-OpenDyslexic.txt and are reproduced in the in-app licenses
screen (app/aboutlibraries/licenses/OpenDyslexic-2.json).

A complete attribution list, the bundled fonts included, is shown in
the application under Settings → About → Open-source licenses. It is
generated from the release dependencies plus the entries in
app/aboutlibraries/, which cover what ships without being one.
